# agent-server — local mode. Copy to .env.local and fill in the two required
# values. `make dev` from the repo root loads this file.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The bearer token the UI sends (Authorization: Bearer …). Any string; the
# desktop app generates one per install and keeps it in the macOS keychain.
SERVER_API_KEY=local-dev-key

# Encrypts provider API keys, MCP secrets and store credentials at rest. Must
# stay the SAME across runs or everything already encrypted becomes unreadable.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
MCP_SECRETS_KEY=

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# External Postgres DSN. EMPTY (or unset) means: start an embedded Postgres 17
# under $DATA_DIR/postgres. That is the normal case; set this only to point at
# a cluster you already run (e.g. docker-compose.dev.yml).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://tasktrooper:tasktrooper@127.0.0.1:5432/tasktrooper?sslmode=disable

# Workspaces, RAG files and the embedded Postgres data directory.
# DATA_DIR=./data

# HTTP port. 0 asks the kernel for a free one; the port that was bound is
# printed to stdout as `LISTENING http://127.0.0.1:<port>`.
# PORT=8085

# Where the embedded Postgres binaries are downloaded and extracted
# (~30 MB, first start only). Default: $DATA_DIR/postgres-bin.
# EMBEDDED_POSTGRES_CACHE_DIR=

# An OpenAI-compatible host exposing POST /v1/embeddings. Set, an embedding
# provider pointing at it (model nomic-embed-text-v1.5, 768 dims) is created at
# boot so RAG and code search work with no clicks. The desktop app sets this to
# its own bundled embedder.
# EMBEDDINGS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1

# Origins allowed to call this server. Default:
#   app://tasktrooper,http://localhost:3200,http://127.0.0.1:3200
# CORS_ORIGINS=

# The origin a Claude Code session calls TaskTrooper's tools back on.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:<port>.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# The Claude Code CLI that runs agents on the claude_code provider. Default:
# whatever `claude` resolves to on PATH.
# CLAUDE_CODE_BIN=

# Chromium for the browser_* tools.
# CHROME_BIN=

# Appium hub for the mobile_* tools.
# MOBILE_APPIUM_HUB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4723

# Set, the server starts that hub itself when a mobile tool needs it and stops
# it after 10 idle minutes; unset, run `appium` yourself.
# APPIUM_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/appium

# How long to keep working after SIGTERM before in-flight agent runs are
# cancelled. Default 9m.
# SHUTDOWN_GRACE=9m

# Seeded into the LLM provider settings on first run, if present.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# Vertex AI instead of a direct endpoint (optional):
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=europe-west1
